/* Test script for GrapaDBX Database-Aware Comparison System */
/* This demonstrates the enhanced comparison logic for different data types and storage models */

"Testing GrapaDBX Database-Aware Comparison System...\n".echo();
"==================================================\n".echo();

/* Test 1: Current Comparison Issues (strcmp for everything) */
"Test 1: Current Comparison Issues (strcmp for everything)\n".echo();
"--------------------------------------------------------\n".echo();

"Current GrapaDB comparison problems:\n".echo();
"• Uses strcmp for all field comparisons\n".echo();
"• Numeric comparisons are incorrect\n".echo();
"• Date/time comparisons are wrong\n".echo();
"• Doesn't understand storage types\n".echo();
"• Complex pointer dereferencing required\n".echo();
"\n".echo();

"Example of current incorrect behavior:\n".echo();
"• Comparing 100 vs 20: strcmp returns '1' (100 < 20) - WRONG!\n".echo();
"• Comparing 5.5 vs 10.2: strcmp returns '1' (5.5 < 10.2) - WRONG!\n".echo();
"• Comparing timestamps: strcmp returns wrong order\n".echo();
"\n".echo();

/* Test 2: Database-Aware Comparison Benefits */
"Test 2: Database-Aware Comparison Benefits\n".echo();
"-----------------------------------------\n".echo();

"GrapaDBX will provide correct comparisons:\n".echo();
"• Type-aware: ALL Grapa data types supported\n".echo();
"• Storage-aware: FIX, VAR, PAR storage handling\n".echo();
"• Tree-aware: ROW, COL, GROUP storage models\n".echo();
"• Index-aware: Multi-field composite indexes\n".echo();
"• Performance: Caching and optimization\n".echo();
"\n".echo();

